WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.117
[MIA] Terry Fawles was sentenced
to death after being convicted

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.658
in a kidnapping incident.

00:00:04.742 --> 00:00:07.075
Two days ago,
he escaped custody.

00:00:07.158 --> 00:00:09.325
While he was free, a
policewoman was murdered,

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:12.492
and her body was found
in the trunk of a stolen car.

00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:14.867
It just so happens that
her testimony is what put him

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.242
away in the first trial,
five years prior.

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:19.325
Believing in his innocence,

00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:21.450
I took to the court
to defend him.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.158
And as I pressed the
eyewitness, Melissa Foster,

00:00:24.242 --> 00:00:26.408
I caught a glimpse of the truth.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.075
[MILES] Okay. But why
would she do all that?

00:00:29.158 --> 00:00:31.408
[MIA] Because she
murdered Valerie Hawthorne,

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:33.658
and then hid the
body in the trunk.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.408
This would also
explain why the body

00:00:35.492 --> 00:00:36.950
was not dumped in the river.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.783
It was all a plot to
frame Mister Fawles!

00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:42.325
[DAHLIA shrieks]

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.700
[MIA] This murder
and the previous

00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:46.492
kidnapping incident
were linked.

00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:48.533
Dahlia... Hawthorne?

00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:50.867
Yeah. That was her name.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.992
The poor little girl who was
kidnapped and murdered

00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:54.492
five years ago.

00:00:54.575 --> 00:00:56.950
She was 14 at the time.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:59.408
Which means that if
she were still alive...

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.658
...she'd be around your age.

00:01:01.742 --> 00:01:02.908
Tell the truth.

00:01:02.992 --> 00:01:06.200
Who are you?
What are you hiding?

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:43.367
[DAHLIA giggles]
Sorry. But may I say something?

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.075
Um, sure, go ahead.

00:02:45.158 --> 00:02:46.492
You're saying
I'm the girl who was

00:02:46.575 --> 00:02:48.158
abducted five years ago?

00:02:48.242 --> 00:02:50.992
Oh, dear. What was
her name again?

00:02:51.075 --> 00:02:53.825
Dahlia Hawthorne. Kuh.

00:02:53.908 --> 00:02:55.450
[MELISSA]
Well that simply cannot be.

00:02:55.533 --> 00:02:56.617
[MIA]
Can you prove this?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.742
[MILES]
Honestly... It's complicated.

00:02:58.825 --> 00:02:59.742
[MIA]
Huh?

00:02:59.825 --> 00:03:01.408
You see, the truth is...

00:03:01.492 --> 00:03:04.283
I was living out of the country
until the year before last.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.242
Yes. She grew up
in a country at war.

00:03:07.325 --> 00:03:09.658
After her parents were killed,
she managed to make

00:03:09.742 --> 00:03:11.117
her way back home alone.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.492
That's right.

00:03:12.575 --> 00:03:15.325
So I don't have anything
that can verify my identity.

00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:17.492
[MIA]
What a contrived sob-story.

00:03:17.575 --> 00:03:19.325
This man held a grudge
and killed the woman

00:03:19.408 --> 00:03:23.242
who testified against him.
The monster.

00:03:23.325 --> 00:03:24.867
Come to think of it,

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.700
I guess I'm lucky I wasn't
wearing a scarf that day.

00:03:27.783 --> 00:03:29.783
[JUDGE 204A]
What do you mean by that?

00:03:29.867 --> 00:03:31.575
[MELISSA] Mister Killer had
forgotten what his target

00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:33.200
looked like, hadn't he?

00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:35.700
If I had worn a white scarf,
I might have been mistaken

00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:38.867
for the officer and
murdered instead!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.325
Hold on, white scarf?

00:03:41.408 --> 00:03:44.908
[MELISSA] Yes, didn't you
mention a scarf earlier?

00:03:44.992 --> 00:03:46.325
Mister Fawles had
trouble remembering

00:03:46.408 --> 00:03:48.325
the victim's appearance.

00:03:48.408 --> 00:03:51.658
That's why he needed the
scarf as a way to identify her.

00:03:51.742 --> 00:03:52.742
Yes, I did.

00:03:52.825 --> 00:03:54.783
But why did you just say
"a white scarf"?

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.242
[MELISSA]
Huh?

00:03:56.325 --> 00:03:58.825
Look at this photo.
Does it look white to you?

00:03:58.908 --> 00:04:00.533
[gasps]

00:04:00.617 --> 00:04:02.617
We have the scarf
in question right here.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.200
And you'll
notice it's not white.

00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:08.992
Okay. But Miss
Victim's memo said--

00:04:09.075 --> 00:04:10.450
[gasps]

00:04:10.533 --> 00:04:12.117
Now you've spilled the beans.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.117
[MIA] Valerie Hawthorne's memo
did say, and I quote:

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.908
"Wear white scarf
for identification."

00:04:17.992 --> 00:04:20.658
The question is,
why do you know about that?

00:04:20.742 --> 00:04:21.658
[DAHLIA whimpers]

00:04:21.742 --> 00:04:23.242
Prosecutor Edgeworth.

00:04:23.325 --> 00:04:26.283
Did you show this witness the
case file sometime before today?

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:29.033
[MILES] No, Your Honor.
I never authorized that.

00:04:29.117 --> 00:04:32.700
I see. Then how did
you know about it?

00:04:32.783 --> 00:04:35.658
For some reason, the witness
knew what the memo said.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.658
But only two people
should have known.

00:04:37.742 --> 00:04:39.783
Mr. Fawles, who gave
the instructions,

00:04:39.867 --> 00:04:42.242
and Valerie Hawthorne,
who wrote it.

00:04:42.325 --> 00:04:43.617
There is one other.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.117
What? Who?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.950
How could you forget?

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.742
Look. She's right there.

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.783
[MIA gasps]
Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:04:55.867 --> 00:04:56.825
Wait. What?

00:04:56.908 --> 00:04:58.408
"Talk to Dahlia."

00:04:58.492 --> 00:05:01.742
I believe I now understand what
those words truly meant.

00:05:01.825 --> 00:05:03.242
Remember?

00:05:03.325 --> 00:05:06.533
The name Dahlia came up in
our discussions not long ago.

00:05:06.617 --> 00:05:08.033
No. You don't mean...

00:05:08.117 --> 00:05:09.700
After Mr. Fawles called her,

00:05:09.783 --> 00:05:11.950
the defendant phoned
somebody else.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.742
Her little sister.
Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:05:14.825 --> 00:05:16.200
[MILES]
Objection!

00:05:16.283 --> 00:05:19.408
That's absurd!
You know as well as I do why.

00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:22.075
Dahlia Hawthorne was
declared dead five years ago!

00:05:22.158 --> 00:05:23.575
[MIA]
True.

00:05:23.658 --> 00:05:25.617
But the fact remains that her
body was never recovered.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.158
[gasps]

00:05:27.242 --> 00:05:28.867
The defense asserts this:

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.867
Our witness,
on the stand right now,

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.908
is the victim of the
incident five years ago.

00:05:33.992 --> 00:05:35.950
Dahlia Hawthorne!

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.367
Wha... What?

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.742
[JURY gasping, murmuring]

00:05:39.825 --> 00:05:41.742
Witness! Just who are you?

00:05:41.825 --> 00:05:42.867
Tell this court!

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.450
You want to know who I am?

00:05:45.533 --> 00:05:47.200
[TERRY]
Hold it!

00:05:47.283 --> 00:05:50.075
[gasps]
Mr. Fawles?

00:05:50.158 --> 00:05:53.492
[TERRY] Dahlia? Is that
really you, Dahlia?

00:05:55.325 --> 00:05:58.117
Mr. Fawles.
It's been five years now.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.950
We should know the
truth! Tell us!

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:02.325
Your Honor!

00:06:02.408 --> 00:06:04.658
I request that the defendant
take the witness stand.

00:06:04.742 --> 00:06:06.658
The court needs to hear
Mr. Fawles' testimony

00:06:06.742 --> 00:06:08.492
about both incidents!

00:06:08.575 --> 00:06:10.575
[JUDGE 204A]
I agree with you.

00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:13.575
What do you say,
Prosecutor Edgeworth?

00:06:13.658 --> 00:06:16.575
The prosecution
has no objections.

00:06:16.658 --> 00:06:17.992
Very well.

00:06:18.075 --> 00:06:20.742
The defendant may
approach the witness stand.

00:06:20.825 --> 00:06:22.158
[TERRY whimpers]

00:06:26.867 --> 00:06:28.575
All right, here we go.

00:06:28.658 --> 00:06:31.658
Yes. I did kidnap Dahlia.

00:06:31.742 --> 00:06:33.867
Five years back.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.283
[VALERIE] Let her go!
Release the hostage now!

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:39.908
There's no way, cop!

00:06:39.992 --> 00:06:42.575
Come closer.
And she's history!

00:06:42.658 --> 00:06:44.533
Ya hear?

00:06:44.617 --> 00:06:46.117
It's the end of the line.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.742
So give up. Or die!

00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:49.908
--[TERRY gasps]
--[gunshot]

00:06:49.992 --> 00:06:52.200
[TERRY]
That woman... She betrayed me!

00:06:52.283 --> 00:06:53.575
Betrayed us!

00:06:53.658 --> 00:06:56.117
[MIA] Betrayed?
What do you mean by that?

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.033
It was fake. All of it.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.617
The kidnapping included.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.533
Huh? What do you mean, "fake"?

00:07:01.617 --> 00:07:03.533
Explain!

00:07:03.617 --> 00:07:08.408
[TERRY]
Dahlia... My angel... My love...

00:07:08.492 --> 00:07:10.617
I'll do anything she says.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.033
Anything Dahlia wants,
I'll give to 'er.

00:07:13.117 --> 00:07:14.075
[thud]

00:07:14.158 --> 00:07:15.825
Wait a second! You don't mean...

00:07:15.908 --> 00:07:17.450
You can't!

00:07:17.533 --> 00:07:20.325
Are you saying the kidnapping
five years ago was planned by...

00:07:20.408 --> 00:07:24.117
Dahlia. And Valerie, too.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.742
What? The victim was in on it?

00:07:26.825 --> 00:07:28.575
[MILES gasps]

00:07:28.658 --> 00:07:30.908
Dahlia's family is super loaded.

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:34.783
They own a jewelry business.
Thought we'd snag a gem.

00:07:34.867 --> 00:07:37.242
Dahlia wrote the kidnap note.

00:07:37.325 --> 00:07:40.325
We asked for a
diamond worth two mil.

00:07:40.408 --> 00:07:43.867
Told 'em to make
the exchange on Dusky Bridge.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:49.617
Told 'em Valerie, Dahlia's
big sister, had to hand it over.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.158
Now we're percolating.

00:07:51.242 --> 00:07:52.700
They thought it was
the perfect crime,

00:07:52.783 --> 00:07:55.200
since they had a cop on
their side to cover it all up.

00:07:55.283 --> 00:07:59.242
But she--Valerie--
betrayed us!

00:07:59.325 --> 00:08:02.325
She shot at me!
Got me right in the arm!

00:08:02.408 --> 00:08:03.325
[gasps]

00:08:03.408 --> 00:08:04.742
And then Dahlia...

00:08:04.825 --> 00:08:06.450
[DAHLIA giggles]

00:08:06.533 --> 00:08:08.867
[TERRY] She jumped
straight in the river.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.617
The diamond was in her backpack.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.783
And I don't know what
happened to her after that.

00:08:13.867 --> 00:08:15.408
[MIA]
To be perfectly clear,

00:08:15.492 --> 00:08:17.200
you're saying she
jumped on purpose?

00:08:17.283 --> 00:08:19.325
[TERRY] Of course,
I couldn'ta pushed her!

00:08:19.408 --> 00:08:21.825
I would never do that to her!

00:08:21.908 --> 00:08:24.950
And that's the bitter,
piping-hot truth, eh?

00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:26.617
Huh.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.700
After she jumped,

00:08:27.783 --> 00:08:30.242
I blacked out from
the gunshot wound.

00:08:30.325 --> 00:08:33.200
Valerie must have arrested
me while I was down.

00:08:33.283 --> 00:08:36.033
And soon afterward,
you were sentenced to death.

00:08:36.117 --> 00:08:38.825
I couldn't forget
that trial if I wanted to!

00:08:38.908 --> 00:08:40.075
[thud]

00:08:40.158 --> 00:08:42.117
[VALERIE] That man
threw her off the bridge!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.825
Straight into the river!

00:08:43.908 --> 00:08:47.908
I saw. It happened!
Right in front of my eyes!

00:08:47.992 --> 00:08:49.575
[TERRY]
These five years,

00:08:49.658 --> 00:08:52.617
it's all I wanted to know
before I died.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.575
Why did she lie like that?

00:08:54.658 --> 00:08:57.117
I had to hear it come
from her own mouth.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.575
[MIA] And that's why you
made such a crazy escape.

00:08:59.658 --> 00:09:04.075
[TERRY whimpers] Yeah. But I
forgot what she looked like,

00:09:04.158 --> 00:09:06.908
so I told her to wear a scarf.

00:09:06.992 --> 00:09:09.825
But... I di'n't murder her!

00:09:09.908 --> 00:09:12.950
I just wanted to know
why she did it.

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:14.908
You're not
getting out of this one.

00:09:14.992 --> 00:09:16.658
You're Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:09:16.742 --> 00:09:17.867
Otherwise, you
couldn't have known

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.825
what was written on the memo!

00:09:19.908 --> 00:09:21.367
[MILES]
Objection!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:22.575
That's enough.

00:09:22.658 --> 00:09:24.283
[MIA]
What do you mean?

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:26.158
[MILES] Now we know
our witness is the victim

00:09:26.242 --> 00:09:30.075
who disappeared five years ago.
Quite the shocking discovery.

00:09:30.158 --> 00:09:32.700
But, that fact has
practically nothing to do

00:09:32.783 --> 00:09:34.033
with the current case.

00:09:34.117 --> 00:09:35.658
[MIA]
How do you figure that?

00:09:35.742 --> 00:09:37.992
There's one important
thing in his testimony.

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:39.742
And only one.

00:09:39.825 --> 00:09:41.658
The sole piece of
information that matters here

00:09:41.742 --> 00:09:44.533
is the fact that the defendant
despised the victim.

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:46.075
[gasps]

00:09:46.158 --> 00:09:47.700
[MILES] The one person with
a motive strong enough to kill

00:09:47.783 --> 00:09:49.908
Valerie Hawthorne
stands before us.

00:09:49.992 --> 00:09:52.658
The defendant, Terry Fawles!

00:09:52.742 --> 00:09:54.408
[MIA]
Objection!

00:09:54.492 --> 00:09:57.200
Prosecutor Edgeworth!
That's not true.

00:09:57.283 --> 00:09:58.658
[MILES grunts]

00:09:58.742 --> 00:10:00.992
Someone else has a strong
motive to murder the victim.

00:10:01.075 --> 00:10:02.575
To cover up her tracks.

00:10:02.658 --> 00:10:04.950
That right? Dahlia Hawthorne?

00:10:07.117 --> 00:10:09.283
If you would be so kind
as to read the rest of the memo

00:10:09.367 --> 00:10:10.783
the victim wrote.

00:10:10.867 --> 00:10:12.783
The rest?

00:10:12.867 --> 00:10:14.283
[MIA]
"Talk to Dahlia.

00:10:14.367 --> 00:10:16.242
Make everything public."

00:10:16.325 --> 00:10:17.783
Yes.

00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:21.200
The victim told you she was
going public about everything.

00:10:21.283 --> 00:10:23.450
She would tell the
world of your crime.

00:10:23.533 --> 00:10:24.783
You two shared this secret,

00:10:24.867 --> 00:10:27.283
and your lives depended
on it being kept.

00:10:27.367 --> 00:10:29.200
So in your mind, you didn't
have much of a choice

00:10:29.283 --> 00:10:33.658
but to kill her. To make sure
she kept quiet forever.

00:10:33.742 --> 00:10:35.492
And what was this
secret between them?

00:10:35.575 --> 00:10:37.242
Let's review what we've heard.

00:10:37.325 --> 00:10:40.742
Five years ago, something else
disappeared along with Dahlia.

00:10:40.825 --> 00:10:42.325
A diamond worth two million,

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:44.658
that had been brought
there as ransom.

00:10:44.742 --> 00:10:46.117
[DAHLIA]
Hmm?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.283
Yes. The fake kidnapping
was a setup from the beginning.

00:10:49.367 --> 00:10:52.200
A trap carefully devised to
frame Mr. Fawles and land

00:10:52.283 --> 00:10:54.908
the two million
in Dahlia's hands!

00:10:54.992 --> 00:10:56.283
Nonsense!

00:10:56.367 --> 00:10:58.783
Five years ago, the witness
was only 14 years old!

00:10:58.867 --> 00:11:00.908
Do you think she was
capable of such a twisted plan?

00:11:00.992 --> 00:11:04.533
I do! Because she
was twisted in her own right!

00:11:04.617 --> 00:11:06.242
And there was
one more person tormented

00:11:06.325 --> 00:11:08.117
by this twisted young girl.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.367
Her older sister,
Valerie Hawthorne!

00:11:12.367 --> 00:11:13.700
This is interesting.

00:11:13.783 --> 00:11:15.992
According to
the case files here,

00:11:16.075 --> 00:11:19.200
Terry Fawles was tutoring
both the Hawthorne girls.

00:11:19.283 --> 00:11:22.200
I bet that's how the
whole relationship started,

00:11:22.283 --> 00:11:25.825
and how he was forced to go
along with his angel's scheme.

00:11:25.908 --> 00:11:27.575
[JUDGE 204A]
I'm not convinced yet.

00:11:27.658 --> 00:11:29.908
She faked her death and
pretended to be someone else

00:11:29.992 --> 00:11:31.450
for five years?

00:11:31.533 --> 00:11:34.617
That seems just a little too
preposterous, don't you think?

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.783
Valerie was a policewoman.

00:11:36.867 --> 00:11:38.783
With her help,
it could've be done.

00:11:38.867 --> 00:11:40.867
She could arrange whatever
paperwork they needed

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.242
without much trouble.

00:11:42.325 --> 00:11:43.533
Yes, but...

00:11:43.617 --> 00:11:45.783
It must have weighed heavily
on her conscience.

00:11:45.867 --> 00:11:48.908
For five years,
she covered up this lie.

00:11:48.992 --> 00:11:51.075
That's why she contacted
her sister immediately

00:11:51.158 --> 00:11:53.200
after Mr. Fawles called her.

00:11:53.283 --> 00:11:55.408
And told her what
she was planning to do.

00:11:55.492 --> 00:11:57.367
She would tell the world.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.450
Or, in the words of
the memo, she was going to

00:12:00.533 --> 00:12:02.033
"make everything public."

00:12:02.117 --> 00:12:03.283
[MIA]
Exactly.

00:12:03.367 --> 00:12:04.992
But the decision to tell
her sister first is what

00:12:05.075 --> 00:12:06.867
ultimately sealed her fate.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.658
Dahlia Hawthorne came up
with yet another twisted plan

00:12:09.742 --> 00:12:11.283
to divert suspicion.

00:12:11.367 --> 00:12:14.200
A plan that would ensure
neither accomplice would talk.

00:12:14.283 --> 00:12:16.533
Frame one and kill the other.

00:12:16.617 --> 00:12:19.408
And that, Your Honor, is
why she murdered her sister,

00:12:19.492 --> 00:12:20.867
Valerie Hawthorne!

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.158
[JURY gasping]

00:12:22.242 --> 00:12:24.450
[JUDGE 204A]
Order! Order in the court!

00:12:24.533 --> 00:12:27.117
[DAHLIA giggles]

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.742
[laughs]

00:12:29.825 --> 00:12:33.200
Um... Why are
you laughing, Miss?

00:12:33.283 --> 00:12:37.200
[DAHLIA] Forgive me.
It's just so comical.

00:12:37.283 --> 00:12:38.742
You're really amusing.

00:12:38.825 --> 00:12:40.450
You know that, Mia Fey?

00:12:41.992 --> 00:12:45.117
[DAHLIA] You can certainly
weave an exciting tale, hag.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.658
But do you have
any proof of your claims?

00:12:47.742 --> 00:12:48.950
Um... Evidence?

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:51.283
Yes, evidence
that I, this inmate here,

00:12:51.367 --> 00:12:54.033
and the policewoman were
all in on it, obviously.

00:12:54.117 --> 00:12:56.242
Without some,
it's just conjecture.

00:12:56.325 --> 00:12:57.242
[MIA]
But it's not.

00:12:57.325 --> 00:12:58.825
[DAHLIA]
The kidnapping was fake?

00:12:58.908 --> 00:13:01.492
I don't know why we should
believe an inmate on death row.

00:13:01.575 --> 00:13:03.242
After all, I'm the victim.

00:13:03.325 --> 00:13:05.783
Yeah, but...
Why did you fake your identity?

00:13:05.867 --> 00:13:07.408
Can you really blame me?

00:13:07.492 --> 00:13:08.950
I mean, I was kidnapped.

00:13:09.033 --> 00:13:11.242
Why wouldn't I want
to go into hiding?

00:13:11.325 --> 00:13:13.200
I was scarred
by the whole thing.

00:13:13.283 --> 00:13:14.450
[JUDGE 204A]
Well, defense?

00:13:14.533 --> 00:13:17.117
If you do have evidence,
now would be the time.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.992
[MIA] It's impossible to
prove that the kidnapping

00:13:19.075 --> 00:13:20.408
was staged now!

00:13:20.492 --> 00:13:22.867
Or prove Terry
didn't murder Valerie.

00:13:24.533 --> 00:13:28.325
The defense has... nothing.

00:13:28.408 --> 00:13:29.408
What a joke!

00:13:29.492 --> 00:13:31.408
You put on that
whole show for nothing?

00:13:31.492 --> 00:13:32.908
Are you stupid?

00:13:32.992 --> 00:13:35.533
[JUDGE 204A] Hmm. It seems
we've reached a conclusion.

00:13:35.617 --> 00:13:37.908
The witness's behavior
does raise suspicions,

00:13:37.992 --> 00:13:40.742
but I'm forced to reject
the defense's assertions.

00:13:40.825 --> 00:13:42.575
Of course you are.

00:13:42.658 --> 00:13:45.533
[MIA]
Is this it? Is it really over?

00:13:47.325 --> 00:13:49.783
This is why you haven't
graduated from cub yet.

00:13:49.867 --> 00:13:50.825
Huh?

00:13:50.908 --> 00:13:52.658
You're a lawyer now.

00:13:52.742 --> 00:13:56.492
Gotta smile no matter how bad
it gets, it's part of the job.

00:13:56.575 --> 00:13:57.742
[gasps]

00:13:57.825 --> 00:13:59.908
[DIEGO] Get a load
of the smirk on her face.

00:13:59.992 --> 00:14:01.867
Electrifying, isn't it?

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.033
That means she's
hiding something big.

00:14:04.117 --> 00:14:06.075
She's ecstatic she
won't be found out.

00:14:06.158 --> 00:14:08.492
Maybe. But we've got no proof.

00:14:08.575 --> 00:14:11.742
[DIEGO] Peh. So without it,
the trial's over?

00:14:11.825 --> 00:14:13.658
Who made that decision?

00:14:13.742 --> 00:14:15.367
What do we do, then?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.867
[DIEGO] To an extent,
you can make your own rules.

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:22.700
Even when there's zero evidence,
there's always testimony.

00:14:22.783 --> 00:14:23.950
[gasps]

00:14:24.033 --> 00:14:26.200
[DIEGO]
So what's our working theory?

00:14:26.283 --> 00:14:28.658
Dahlia Hawthorne
killed her sister Valerie,

00:14:28.742 --> 00:14:32.283
hid her body in the trunk,
disguised herself as her,

00:14:32.367 --> 00:14:35.242
and met Fawles on Dusky Bridge.

00:14:35.325 --> 00:14:37.533
Is that about right so far?

00:14:37.617 --> 00:14:39.658
[MIA]
Yes, that's right.

00:14:39.742 --> 00:14:42.575
In which case,
the answer's obvious to me.

00:14:42.658 --> 00:14:45.283
We've still got a man on
the witness stand after all.

00:14:45.367 --> 00:14:46.283
[MIA gasps]

00:14:46.367 --> 00:14:47.325
Uh... What's up?

00:14:47.408 --> 00:14:48.533
You've heard it all.

00:14:48.617 --> 00:14:50.783
Have you anything to say?
We need you!

00:14:50.867 --> 00:14:52.283
[TERRY whimpers]

00:14:52.367 --> 00:14:53.617
Listen to me.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.992
I don't know what she said
to you five years ago.

00:14:56.075 --> 00:14:59.158
But Dahlia Hawthorne
is very much alive.

00:14:59.242 --> 00:15:02.908
She used you!
And for what, money?

00:15:02.992 --> 00:15:04.992
That can't be...

00:15:05.075 --> 00:15:07.742
If the defense cannot
present evidence of their claim,

00:15:07.825 --> 00:15:09.492
this trial need not continue.

00:15:09.575 --> 00:15:10.867
[MIA]
Please wait!

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.908
Mr. Fawles! This is
our final chance!

00:15:13.992 --> 00:15:16.075
You have to tell us
who you met on Dusky Bridge

00:15:16.158 --> 00:15:17.533
two days ago!

00:15:17.617 --> 00:15:20.992
Try to remember their face!
Was it Valerie or Dahlia?

00:15:21.075 --> 00:15:22.992
Testify to the court!

00:15:23.075 --> 00:15:25.950
[TERRY whimpes]

00:15:26.033 --> 00:15:26.950
[DAHLIA]
Terry.

00:15:27.033 --> 00:15:28.075
[TERRY]

00:15:30.658 --> 00:15:31.575
[TERRY]
Dahlia?

00:15:31.658 --> 00:15:34.283
Yes. It's been a while.

00:15:34.367 --> 00:15:38.658
I hate to ask, but you
didn't betray me, did you?

00:15:38.742 --> 00:15:40.492
I don't need to say anything.

00:15:40.575 --> 00:15:42.242
Don't you know the answer?

00:15:42.325 --> 00:15:43.450
[gasps]

00:15:43.533 --> 00:15:46.158
Careful, my life is
in your hands right now.

00:15:46.242 --> 00:15:48.992
Oh. Dahlia...

00:15:49.075 --> 00:15:50.700
Are you okay?

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:52.033
Miss Lawyer lady?

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:53.575
[MIA]
Uh... Yes?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.700
Sorry. My throat's dry.

00:15:56.783 --> 00:15:59.033
Could I get some water?

00:15:59.117 --> 00:16:00.492
I've got more coffee.

00:16:00.575 --> 00:16:03.533
If you don't mind a substitute.

00:16:03.617 --> 00:16:06.575
It's a good fit for
your current situation.

00:16:06.658 --> 00:16:08.117
Bitter and darker than hell.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.158
Just like what
you're about to say.

00:16:19.283 --> 00:16:21.575
You sure know
how to enjoy a cup.

00:16:21.658 --> 00:16:23.367
All right, defendant.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.200
Make your final statement.

00:16:25.283 --> 00:16:27.075
That day... 4 PM.

00:16:27.158 --> 00:16:29.617
I stopped the car
just before Dusky Bridge.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.117
And got out.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:34.200
She wasn't there yet,
so I decided to wait

00:16:34.283 --> 00:16:38.408
on the bridge itself.
It was our meeting place.

00:16:38.492 --> 00:16:41.742
Finally, a woman showed up.

00:16:41.825 --> 00:16:44.033
And it was...

00:16:44.117 --> 00:16:46.200
It was Valerie, no doubt!

00:16:46.283 --> 00:16:47.492
Mr. Fawles!

00:16:47.575 --> 00:16:50.492
It was her! Not Dahlia, okay?

00:16:50.575 --> 00:16:52.533
How can you still cover for her?

00:16:52.617 --> 00:16:54.575
After all she's done to you!

00:16:54.658 --> 00:16:56.200
Well, you heard it yourself.

00:16:56.283 --> 00:16:58.575
It's clear. The defense's
claims were baseless,

00:16:58.658 --> 00:16:59.867
as we've all likely guessed.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.575
[MIA]
Is this what you want?

00:17:01.658 --> 00:17:04.492
You'll be found guilty, and
you'll go back to death row!

00:17:04.575 --> 00:17:06.200
He's under the girl's curse.

00:17:06.283 --> 00:17:07.950
I think he's a lost cause.

00:17:08.033 --> 00:17:11.117
He'll probably believe her until
he's buried six feet under.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.492
But I...

00:17:12.575 --> 00:17:15.283
But you still have a
duty to press him for the truth.

00:17:15.367 --> 00:17:19.492
That's our curse. The one
we bear as defense attorneys.

00:17:21.783 --> 00:17:24.075
[MIA] According to the memo,
you were supposed to meet

00:17:24.158 --> 00:17:25.742
at 4:30 PM.

00:17:25.825 --> 00:17:28.325
You arrived awfully early,
don't you think?

00:17:28.408 --> 00:17:32.200
Did you wait on the bridge
a full 30 minutes?

00:17:32.283 --> 00:17:34.533
Terry?

00:17:34.617 --> 00:17:37.283
[TERRY] I got there
around 4 PM like I said.

00:17:37.367 --> 00:17:39.700
But didn't stick around
the bridge the whole time.

00:17:39.783 --> 00:17:42.658
I had somewhere to go.
Someplace special.

00:17:42.742 --> 00:17:45.158
[MIA]
Someplace special? Like where?

00:17:45.242 --> 00:17:47.283
There's this old temple,
a 15 minute walk

00:17:47.367 --> 00:17:50.158
from the bridge.
The path's too narrow for a car.

00:17:50.242 --> 00:17:54.408
There, five years ago,
me and Dahlia made a promise.

00:17:54.492 --> 00:17:56.825
We swore to
never betray each other,

00:17:56.908 --> 00:17:58.783
and always believe
in each other.

00:17:58.867 --> 00:18:02.492
And she gave me a memento
to represent our vow.

00:18:02.575 --> 00:18:04.533
She did? Is that so?

00:18:04.617 --> 00:18:05.867
[TERRY]
Back then...

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:09.033
...I hid it under the base
of a tree around there.

00:18:09.117 --> 00:18:12.325
It's a real
special memory for me.

00:18:12.408 --> 00:18:16.658
So... I went there to get it.

00:18:16.742 --> 00:18:18.492
Your Honor, you heard my client.

00:18:18.575 --> 00:18:20.325
He was away for 30 minutes.

00:18:20.408 --> 00:18:22.617
Fifteen minutes
there, 15 back.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.492
Meaning, the car was
unattended that whole time.

00:18:25.575 --> 00:18:28.033
So. There was time to frame him.

00:18:28.117 --> 00:18:30.783
Valerie could have arrived
while Mr. Fawles was gone.

00:18:30.867 --> 00:18:33.033
And Dahlia could have
murdered her and hid her body

00:18:33.117 --> 00:18:34.033
in the trunk.

00:18:34.117 --> 00:18:35.533
It's possible!

00:18:35.617 --> 00:18:38.825
[sighs] How much more time
are you planning to waste today?

00:18:38.908 --> 00:18:41.533
Mr. Fawles. Do you
think that's what happened?

00:18:41.617 --> 00:18:43.617
[pants]

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:44.992
[MIA]
What's wrong?

00:18:45.075 --> 00:18:45.992
[TERRY coughs]

00:18:46.075 --> 00:18:47.367
[MIA gasps]
Mr. Fawles!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.450
[TERRY whimpers]
Think...

00:18:49.533 --> 00:18:50.617
...I'm done...

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.367
[gasps]
That's blood!

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:53.908
Did he...?

00:18:53.992 --> 00:18:56.825
[TERRY] Five years ago,
at the old temple tree...

00:18:56.908 --> 00:19:01.283
...we promised to trust
each other until death...

00:19:01.367 --> 00:19:04.450
If we can't trust
each other no more,

00:19:04.533 --> 00:19:06.117
there's one thing to do--

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.408
Drink the bottle.

00:19:09.117 --> 00:19:11.950
[gasps]
Mr. Fawles!

00:19:12.033 --> 00:19:13.492
--[JURY gasping, chattering]
--This can't be happening!

00:19:13.575 --> 00:19:15.408
Your Honor!
We need a recess, now!

00:19:15.492 --> 00:19:18.367
Bailiffs, go!
Call the medics! Hurry!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:21.325
[TERRY whimpers]

00:19:21.408 --> 00:19:24.033
I'm such... an idiot...

00:19:24.117 --> 00:19:27.283
I couldn't keep...
my promise to my love...

00:19:27.367 --> 00:19:29.658
No! We're this close, Terry!

00:19:29.742 --> 00:19:31.367
This close to
proving your innocence!

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.450
We're almost there!
Please, just--

00:19:33.533 --> 00:19:36.450
Yah know, even if I'm innocent,

00:19:36.533 --> 00:19:38.367
I don't trust myself...

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.992
Maybe one day,
I'll accidentally...

00:19:41.075 --> 00:19:44.325
...kill my Dahlia... again...

00:19:44.408 --> 00:19:47.117
[gasps]

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.117
Thanks for the... coffee...

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:51.617
It really helped...

00:19:53.117 --> 00:19:54.283
[rasps]

00:19:56.033 --> 00:19:58.200
[gasps]
No, Mr. Fawles!

00:19:58.283 --> 00:20:02.117
Mr. Fawles?! Please, hang on!
You're almost free!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.325
Please Mr. Fawles, no!

00:20:23.867 --> 00:20:26.533
[DIEGO] Inexcusable.
The truth was right there

00:20:26.617 --> 00:20:29.992
in front of our faces.
But we couldn't grasp it.

00:20:30.075 --> 00:20:32.158
I guess we were just too soft.

00:20:32.242 --> 00:20:35.283
It's not your fault.
But it is mine.

00:20:35.367 --> 00:20:37.492
If I were better...

00:20:37.575 --> 00:20:41.950
[sobs] I knew it! I knew
I wasn't cut out for this!

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:46.950
[DIEGO]
Mia...

00:20:47.033 --> 00:20:48.825
[gasps]

00:20:48.908 --> 00:20:50.658
[DIEGO]
I understand how you feel.

00:20:50.742 --> 00:20:53.408
But you can't cry yet.

00:20:53.492 --> 00:20:55.033
Remember this:

00:20:58.617 --> 00:21:02.283
[DIEGO] It's only okay
to cry when it's all over.

00:21:02.367 --> 00:21:04.158
[gasps]
Mr. Armando?

00:21:05.825 --> 00:21:07.033
[MILES gasps]

00:21:10.825 --> 00:21:11.992
[PHOENIX]
And just like that,

00:21:12.075 --> 00:21:14.325
Mia's first trial
came to an end.

00:21:14.408 --> 00:21:16.825
It left no winners
or losers in its wake.

00:21:16.908 --> 00:21:20.158
Only a deep wound in the hearts
of a young defense attorney

00:21:20.242 --> 00:21:21.533
and prosecutor.

00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:25.867
[PHOENIX]
A year after this trial,

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:29.033
I got wrapped up in
a separate incident.

00:21:29.117 --> 00:21:32.033
The fateful case that
brought me and Mia together.

00:21:32.117 --> 00:21:35.033
Only after that did Dahlia
Hawthorne finally get punished

00:21:35.117 --> 00:21:37.450
for her heinous crimes.

00:21:37.533 --> 00:21:39.242
She was declared guilty.

00:21:39.325 --> 00:21:42.033
Yet even in that moment,
she still had a perfect,

00:21:42.117 --> 00:21:45.200
angelic smile on her face.

00:21:45.283 --> 00:21:47.033
At last, it was all over.

00:21:47.117 --> 00:21:49.700
At least, that's what
I thought at the time.

00:21:49.783 --> 00:21:52.075
Unfortunately,
it was wishful thinking.

00:21:52.158 --> 00:21:53.992
And five years later...

00:21:54.075 --> 00:21:56.658
...I would come to learn
just how wrong I was.

00:23:19.992 --> 00:23:21.492
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:21.575 --> 00:23:23.742
To help Maya train,
Pearl and I join her

00:23:23.825 --> 00:23:27.033
on a trip to a spiritual
retreat at Hazakura Temple.

00:23:27.117 --> 00:23:28.950
There, we meet
a nun named Iris,

00:23:29.033 --> 00:23:31.242
who looks exactly
like Dahlia Hawthorne.

00:23:31.325 --> 00:23:34.908
And trust me, I'm not mistaken.
I'd never forget that face.

00:23:34.992 --> 00:23:37.992
There has to be a huge secret
hidden here, I just know it!

00:23:38.075 --> 00:23:40.575
The curtain rises
on our biggest case yet!

00:23:40.658 --> 00:23:43.367
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:46.492
Next episode: "Bridge
to the Turnabout--1st Trial"!

00:23:46.575 --> 00:23:47.658
Take that!
